{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560318-why-no-greater-wan-kueis-battled-the-ravnos-in-week-of-nightmare-like-arhats","id":1560318,"title":"Why no greater Wan Kueis battled the Ravnos in Week of Nightmare? Like Arhats?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-06-02T21:45:12-07:00","id":1560318,"title":"Why no greater Wan Kueis battled the Ravnos in Week of Nightmare? Like Arhats?","content":"Though many arhats are hermits, but iirc there\u2019s at least one for each dharma, keeps an eye on the world (Thrashing Dragon and Bone Flower book already have 1 each). When the world is almost fucked up by a powerful Yama King, how can they really do nothing and let it go? Devil-Tiger\u2019s tenets perfectly support this kind of armageddon war<br /> <br /> The 3 bodhisattvas fought him are powerful ones of course (the Devil-Tiger one maybe the one of the most powerful bodhi alive), but more important, they\u2019re a bit active and far from retired<br /> <br /> Edit: That legendary shih demon hunter god slayer maybe also an option","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 06-03-2026, 03:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-02T22:29:14-07:00","id":1560319,"title":"","content":"Supposedly, getting to the big 10 on your Dharma makes them incredibly likely to just start passing on from this world into whatever post-Hungry Dead state awaits them. So they might be kind of half-faded or likely to just disappear the moment they wake up or act in any significant capacity. Unlike Antediluvians, there was never really much word count devoted to the capacities of arhats, with the above assumption likely contributing to why. Hence, no extensive and creepy text extolling their powers, comparing them to deities, hyping up their plot device powers, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-02T22:30:18-07:00","id":1560320,"title":"","content":"It's been a long time since I last read it, but I recall there was a prophecy that said that a great demon would wake up and 3 elder Bodhisattvas would go fight and defeat him and then go on to do other stuff afterwards. So the three Bodhisattvas showed up to fight him except in the middle of the battle everyone got killed by the Technocratic space lasers. This was not what was supposed to happen and certain segments of the Wan Kuei community were having a crisis of faith as they were trying to reconcile with the fact that their prophecy kind of fell on its face.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-02T23:54:56-07:00","id":1560321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560318-why-no-greater-wan-kueis-battled-the-ravnos-in-week-of-nightmare-like-arhats?p=1560320#post1560320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's been a long time since I last read it, but I recall there was a prophecy that said that a great demon would wake up and 3 elder Bodhisattvas would go fight and defeat him and then go on to do other stuff afterwards. So the three Bodhisattvas showed up to fight him except in the middle of the battle everyone got killed by the Technocratic space lasers. This was not what was supposed to happen and certain segments of the Wan Kuei community were having a crisis of faith as they were trying to reconcile with the fact that their prophecy kind of fell on its face.</div> </div> </div> </div>Related in the Nagah book, of all places.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-03T11:08:23-07:00","id":1560322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560318-why-no-greater-wan-kueis-battled-the-ravnos-in-week-of-nightmare-like-arhats?p=1560319#post1560319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Supposedly, getting to the big 10 on your Dharma makes them incredibly likely to just start passing on from this world into whatever post-Hungry Dead state awaits them. So they might be kind of half-faded or likely to just disappear the moment they wake up or act in any significant capacity.</div> </div> </div> </div>This^<br /> Wan Kues aren't like vampires where they just become ever more of a raid-boss. On the rare occasions when they reach full enlightenment, they actually peace-out and go to Heaven. They Rube-Goldberg their way to the fate regular humans get just by living a decent life. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-03T11:45:09-07:00","id":1560324,"title":"","content":"If I may add<br /> Because when a Kuei-jin reaches Arhat status, they shed their undead curse, break free from the cycle of unlife, and ascend to the <b>Hundred Clouds</b><br /> A few postpone the ascension but there is exactly one canonical Arhat who actively refused to leave the Earthly plane. Her name is <b>The Most Serene Black Pearl Mistress</b>, a master of the <i>Song of the Shadow</i> Dharma<br /> <b>Thousand Crane Mother</b>, the revered Arhat and spiritual progenitor of the Dance of the Thrashing Dragon Dharma was also around but she is a bit of a wild card, more of a legend (she do exist and became depressed whe nher favorite pupil, Black Earth Boy died and technically dropped back from Dharma 10 to 9)<br /> <br /> So basically just two were around at the near end of the Fifth Age, when the Week of Nightmares happened<br /> <br /> But the Keui-jin had several Bodhisattvas... yet why just three?<br /> <br /> Simple<br /> Because none of the great Dharmas actually <i>require </i>you to wage a war against the Yama Kings or the Forces of Yomi<br /> Yomi and the Yama Kings are the part of the Celestial Order, part of the system<br /> And the Wheel Must Turn - that means the Demon Emperor must rise, that will be the start of the Sixth Age and the defeat of the Demon Emperor will signal the start of the Seventh Age<br /> So the funny situation is: the Yama Kings work hard to hasten the arrival of the Sixth Age, many belive one of their members will be the Demon Emperor... and of course the Demon Emepror would want to stop the Wheel to rule forever<br /> But the Yama Kings are not fools... they know, when the Demon Emperor rises and the world become literal Hell, they will be <i>under</i> the Demon Emperor, serving<br /> ...and neither of them want to serve or be slaves so none of the Yama King actually want the Wheel to stuck in the Sixth Age and have an eternity serving and fearing the Demon Emperor<br /> Lord of Centipede, the entity who is the Wyrm in the eyes of the Hengeyokai (and the Kuei-jin - as an interesting side note, they also belive the great dragon of balance and harmony wanted to bless the Tapestry, just got too close and it pulled him in, he paniced and started to trash around as he entangled in the threads, tearing out chunks of the Tapestry [that later became Malfeas] after managed to get out, he hid himself in shame and without his presence the Blanace and Harmony also lessened in the world giving space to corruption and such things. Some tales say he is hiding in the realm of his brother, the Ebon Dragon. This tale is eerily similar to how the Wyrm got trapped, and many belive the bottom of the Dark Umbra, Oblivion is the mouht of the Wyrm... just a funny little lore tidbit) just wants to coil around and shatter the Wheel and the Demons of Yomi not always the allies of the minons of Lord of Centipede...<br /> It is a complicated<br /> <br /> So back to the point<br /> \u200b\u200bNone of the great Dharmas actually <i>require </i>you to wage a war against the Yama Kings, they are enemies, if you serve them? That is a death sentance, you became an Akuma. But small deals here and there? Learning from demons, as long as you reamain loyal to the Court and your Wu? Or to the Havens? It is okay. Especially because the Yama Kings are not always working together and a clever little Kuei-jin, risking the attention of Yomi, can navigate, playing them against each other. Risky but not strickly against the rules<br /> Even the Devil-Tigers who seek to master their own inner demons ultimately want replace the Yama Kings to restore proper cosmic justice while usualyl in the front lines when they are young and destroy Demons are not always at war with Yomi.<br /> They want to replace them and sure that could mean destroying them, but by Havenly Mandate lesser demons bow their heads already before the Devil-Tigers and serve them. And ehen you consider there are still Yama Kings who are still fullfiling their duty give nto them by the August Personage of Jade, like Haha No Fukami, the Mother of the Depths, the &quot;Empress of Pearls&quot; who was the primal ocean mother during the First Age, but changed to her current duty at the request of the August Personage of Jade? It is not that simple.<br /> <br /> So while the Ravnos were a thorn in the side of the Kuei-jin that conflict was not widespread, not a &quot;global&quot; thing. More like a local war that lasted a few Ages but mostly happened in India especially bothering the Infintie Thounder Court and other local Courts<br /> The Bodhisattvas of others? The Five August Courts of the Quincunx probably smiled with glee seeing the indian &quot;brothers&quot; who just gave them headache struggles and unless it involved them somehow? Not really bothered to help.<br /> The Uji of Japan? The Green Court of Korea? The Golden Courts of Malaysia, Vietnam, Laos and Thailand?<br /> The Golden Lion Court of Singapore?<br /> Same<br /> <br /> And here comes the magician's trick!<br /> Black Earth Boy, Rising Majestically to the Western Sun, and Eight Thunders Sage marched to face Zapataashura not because they were particularly keen about the idea, or wanted the best for the world<br /> They did it, because it was <i>prophesied</i><br /> The three of them were fated to stand as a holy vanguard to fight, banish, and eventually defeat a very powerful Demon-King<br /> Not the Demon Emperor, but something very dangerous<br /> They never ment to stop the rise of the Demon Emperor, they never belived what they are fated to fight against will the one who claim the tittle - after all, they were destined to fight and ideally won <br /> They not even tought what they will face will be a Yama King at all - sure, the nightmares that week usually featured the <i>Demon-King Ravana</i>\u200b but...<br /> ...but the Kuei-jin actually were <i>aware</i>, Ravana is out of the Game! His Kingdom in Yomi, Lanka was ruined, his Rakshas barely been able to hold it together; he largely abandoned his city and withdrew into his scorched palace. Hanuman (the Kitsune and the Nuwisha both claim Hanuman as one of their own, though the legends suggest that Hanuman was a monkey) torched the whole place with holy white fire. It is a minor miracle Ravana' s general, the Raksha Thratri not replaced him (under Thratri' s command , the rakshas work together with a coherence they never had under Ravana and many observers wondered if Thratri was destined to usurp Ravana's place and become the next great Yama Queen)<br /> Only when India tested its first nuclear weapon in 1998, May 12, dragged him out of his depression and he stirred - but only because He believes he knows how to harvest the souls of the nuclear dead. - okay this last one the Kuei-jin not know, but it is not that important actually just worth to mention<br /> <br /> The Week of Nightmares was a big thing, but fro mthe Kuei-Jin point of view:<br /> -It was a local problem<br /> -They had a prophecy who and when have to face some ancient evil<br /> -Even the worst case scenario eg. that ancient evil claims the title of the Demon Emperor and the Sixth Age begin... is just part of the Celestial Order. The Wheel must turn. The Fifth Age have to end sooner or later, the Sixth must come, the Demon Emperor must rise.. becaue his fall will herald tha begining of the Seventh Age when things slowly starting to become better and better\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 06-03-2026, 03:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-03T12:52:40-07:00","id":1560325,"title":"","content":"The true identity of Ravana and whether Ravana and Ravnos are the same being has always been up in the air. During the Week of Nightmares, Ravnos and Ravana were said to be one and the same, and psychics seeing visions of the Ravnos antedeluvian battling the Bodhisattvas specifically heard the name Ravana. But then later in the Ravnos clanbook, which released after the Week of Nightmares material, it's stated that Ravana was <i>not</i> Ravnos, but one of Ravnos' childer, who chose to throw in with demons, and eventually after becoming a Yama King, Ravana showed up to taunt Ravnos.<br /> <br /> Personally, I have always threaded the needle by saying Ravnos split his soul into his Hun and Po, which seems like something one could reasonably do with plot level Animalism. His higher soul became Ravana, a Yama King and his lower soul (his Beast) slumbered in his body until it eventually awoke up and went berserk during the Week of Nightmares.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-04T00:12:59-07:00","id":1560333,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560318-why-no-greater-wan-kueis-battled-the-ravnos-in-week-of-nightmare-like-arhats?p=1560325#post1560325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I have always threaded the needle by saying Ravnos split his soul into his Hun and Po, which seems like something one could reasonably do with plot level Animalism. His higher soul became Ravana, a Yama King and his lower soul (his Beast) slumbered in his body until it eventually awoke up and went berserk during the Week of Nightmares.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice idea!<br /> I love it<br /> <br /> While I <i>usually</i> treat them a speperate entity and prefer the version where Ravana was Zapathasura's children (and sometimes the Ravnos a whole not Cainites at all, but like how the <i>Karavalanisha Vrana</i> suggested, a seperate breed of cursed monsters. Zapathasura and his brood are a quasi-failed Wan Xian 2.0; he was indeed someone the Gods created to be a weapon anaginst the <i>asuratizayya</i> or &quot;countless demons&quot; just they not really did a great job, so abandoned the procejt and the Scarlet Phoenix and the Ebon Dragon tired the third time creating champions to protect Huamnity, this time the Hunters. Success may vary) who turned to Yomi, embraced the demonic powers of infernalism and carved out a nice place for himself in Yomi, became a Yama King - something a simple mortal manage to do, it is not that hard, Mikaboshi was a Human infernalist geomancer, a <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Japan_(WOD)\" target=\"_blank\">j</a>apanese scholar and fang shih... the bar is not <i>that </i>high - I used something similar you described but with Zapathasura having Protean, following the Tale of the Spider King and the Tiger Queen.<br /> In that version Zapathasura/Churka and Ennoia were twins/broodmates, so they shared a Sire (if you want to be funny, the 2nd Generation Ravnos, from the OG legend, Embraced by Kaen/Caine) thus both shared the Discipline, just Zapathasura not passed it down on his line (tho' worth to mention several ancient Ravnos displayed Protean-like powers).<br /> So Zapathasura split himself into two version, with the Level 9 Protean power called Dual Form - Zapatashura, who became thus 4th Generation (and that would actually explain why it was even possible him to die... if he died) and Ravana, the Demon King of Lanka who became a Demon<br /> <br /> The reason why he did this in that story of mine?<br /> The War started to become really ugly and the kids started to truning against him; it was a fail-safe because while the two versions are magically linked, if one of the bodies is killed, the other body does not automatically die. And this way he freely could explore those dark, forbidden secrets and powers in his Ravana body, while the Zapathasura verison explore the vampiric possibilities (and in this scenario the main reason of the Ravnos-Gangrel enmity existed , because Zapathasura belived his soul was already split at birth and his twin, Ennoia had it. Eating her would not only restored his 3rd gen status, but would made him whole again)<br /> <br /> (Also if you want to be really cruel, give them the Draught of Phoenix Blood protean power too)<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-04T11:36:38-07:00","id":1560350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560318-why-no-greater-wan-kueis-battled-the-ravnos-in-week-of-nightmare-like-arhats?p=1560333#post1560333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Embraced by Kaen/Caine<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>NB: The Biblical figure has an official rendering in Chinese and it doesn't look or sound much like the attempts that White Wolf made - (traditional script: <b>\u8a72\u96b1</b>), which is read in Mandarin as Gaiyin, in Cantonese as Goijan (j is a y in jyutping romanization), and Southern Min as Kai-un.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-04T23:31:48-07:00","id":1560361,"title":"","content":"<br /> Yeah, on the other hand the members of the Powara, the nomadic family of mortals and kinfolk that Caine joined - well according the Ravnos - originally were the wanderers and outcasts of the First City, the City that was located in the Land of Nod; in turn, Land of Nod was located east of Eden<br /> I will not bore you with details how to find it based the hints and little things scattered around in the supplements, but safe to say, the Land of Nod was somewhere the area of today's Afghanistan and Pakistan<br /> Caine shared the story of the fall of the First City with them<br /> <br /> Now there is a ~3000 years gap between the First and the Second City with an added bonus of the Deluge<br /> <br /> Interestingly this fits nicely into the little story that popped up in both the Thousad Hells and Land of Eigh Million Dreams how in the Age of Legends (the Third Age) the Yama Kings fooled the Dragon Great Dragon, Kung Kung and caused the Deluge. The Hsien managed to stop the flood before was too late and extinguished all life and Kung Kung was so ashamed he left the Heavens and hid in the Kun Lun Mountains, never to cause trouble again (later he came back from his exile during the Dragon River Wars an Age later in the Fourth Age thanks to Yi, the Archer)<br /> The Powara came to the Second City and made camp outside its walls; at this time Ravnos was already Embraced by Caine/Kaen and Embraced at least one other person from whom the Ravnos originates (ideally Churka and/or Zapatahsura) aside Ennoia who betryed him and he ended up dailed to the roof of the great temple of the Second City<br /> Now the exact geographical coordinates of the Second City are deliberately unmapped and left a mystery, but it is generally established as being located in somewhere Mesopotamia; modern-day Iraq/Syria<br /> I'm not sure, given these areas - tho the Land of Nod basically was the part of the Middle Kingdom or at least was on the border to be effected by the &quot;laws of the Middle Kingdom and the Yama Kings&quot; probably, even if that border tend to shift and move it seems - White Wolf really wanted Caine/Kaen to sound anything the official rendering in Chinese should sound<br /> <br /> Especially since the Powara in theory been the members/ancestors of the Roma people; originated from northern India, specifically from the region that is today the Punjab and their language originated in the Indian subcontinent with historical proximity to Sanskrit and Hindi<br /> Linguists and historians trace the word &quot;Rom&quot; back to the Sanskrit word <b>Doma</b>. In ancient and medieval India, the Doma were an established nomadic sub-group. They were first documented in classical Indian texts as traveling musicians, dancers, and metalworkers<br /> Now the farthes you can go with this is around 200 BC so lets just say, White Wolf dump stat was either intellgience or wisdom when made these connections because the Second City flourished in roughly between 7300 BCE and 5600 BCE.<br /> <br /> While it is fun to try to make sense, usually (9 ot of 10 times...) you will just fall in some historical inconistency<br /> But I still like to make a coherent quasi-correct time line of events... but lets say, it is not always a sucessful atempt<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}